//! Golden test of `StructureTemplate` against the real vanilla class (fixture `tests/fixtures/structure_template_place.txt.gz`,
//! generated by `tests/oracle/StructureTemplateOracle.java`): the static transform math, and `placeInWorld` of every template of
//! the vanilla data pack over the synthetic world of the feature harness with rotations, mirrors, pivots, bounding boxes,
//! liquid/known-shape/entity settings, a shared settings random, every processor list of the data pack and the other
//! processor types. Each scenario compares the `placeInWorld` result, the template queries (`getSize`, `getBoundingBox`,
//! `getJigsaws`, `filterBlocks`), the next value of the random argument and digests of the dump lines of every chunk
//! (changed blocks, block entity NBT, heightmaps, post-processing marks, ticks, region random).
//!
//! `STRUCTURE_TEMPLATE_STRIDE=n` runs every n-th scenario only (default 1 = all), `STRUCTURE_TEMPLATE_ONLY=id` one scenario
//! and prints its dump (compare with `scripts/vanilla-java.sh .../StructureTemplateOracle.java out.txt <template> <id>`).


